    Returns an output of type: string
- list_years_for_metric_tool: List all years for which *metric_name* has stored data.
    Takes inputs: {'metric_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The metric of interest (case-insensitive).'}}
    Returns an output of type: array
- get_metric_value_tool: Return the stored value (in *thousands* of USD) for *metric_name* in *year*.
    Takes inputs: {'metric_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the financial metric to look up.'}, 'year': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Four-digit calendar year (e.g. ``2016``).'}}
    Returns an output of type: integer
- calculate_difference_tool: Compute **minuend − subtrahend**.
    Takes inputs: {'minuend': {'type': 'number', 'description': 'The value from which *subtrahend* will be subtracted.'}, 'subtrahend': {'type': 'number', 'description': 'The value to subtract.'}}
    Returns an output of type: number
- calculate_percentage_change_tool: Compute the percentage change from *old_value* to *new_value*.

The formula is ``((new_value − old_value) / old_value) * 100`` and the
function returns the result formatted like ``"13.5%"`` (one decimal place
plus a percent sign).
    Takes inputs: {'old_value': {'type': 'number', 'description': 'Baseline value (denominator in the calculation).'}, 'new_value': {'type': 'number', 'description': 'Comparison value (numerator in the calculation).'}}
    Returns an output of type: string
- sum_metric_across_years_tool: Return the total of *metric_name* across all available years (primarily a distractor).
    Takes inputs: {'metric_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The metric whose values you wish to aggregate.'}}
    Returns an output of type: integer
- final_answer: Provides a final answer to the given problem.
    Takes inputs: {'answer': {'type': 'any', 'description': 'The final answer to the problem'}}
    Returns an output of type: any

